ong  time you know I don't see all the  comments that come in don't don't leave  a comment on if you I mean leave a  comment on the videos but it doesn't  mean as much anymore as it used to right  because we get so many so we're spoiled  so the big the big creators don't worry  about it you can it's always good karma  that's to spread positivity but if you  had to pick  pick for the smaller ones  because just one person saying I see you  just one person saying thank you just  one person saying this message meant  something to me this just one just one  person  having that belief  is the difference quite often between  them quitting and them following through  your single message today to somebody  is going to be the difference I promise  you for somebody if you did that every  day it will for sure be the difference  for quite a number of people between  them quitting and then continuing on  because you took 15 seconds to send a  quick message to them  so Big Y little Y and then pay it  forward especially to the small creators  we got to get out of the Sleepwalk guys  we we want to feel like we matter we  want to feel like today matters we want  to feel like the work we do matters and  the best way that you can inspire people  you want to help the people around you  you want to help your community you want  to help your family you want to help the  people who might see you you want to  help people the best way to help them is  for you to stop sleepwalking is for you  to start doing things that matter it's  not for you to just  make a inspirational video  it's through your actions that if you  showed up today and decided that you're  going to remember your big why that  you're going to serve with your little  why that you're going to pay it forward  to other people  when you see the impact that that can  have on their life  it makes you reconnect to why you do  what you do  and if you woke up and did the thing  that made you remember why you do what  you do and you felt it not just words  you're telling yourself but you  genuinely felt it  holy cow look out because life starts to  get really really good  if you think money is scarce you hoard  it because you believe that no more  money will come to you  if you know money is abundant more money  will flow to you this isn't about being  wasteful doesn't it doesn't mean you  have to go and always empty your pockets  and buy a lot of dumb stuff and throw  away all your other stuff it doesn't  mean you have to waste your money  but it's switching the mindset of money  is not just some scarce thing that you  don't know how to make that you will  never have more of and so you need to  hoard every single dollar that you've  got  this is honestly something that I am  continuing to rewire myself on I  struggled a lot with money especially in  the early days of my business  um even growing up I grew up in a middle  class family my parents spent my parents  are behind me on the wall hold on there  we go this is me when I'm eight or nine  and my parents here they believed in  education a lot and they didn't have a  ton of money we weren't poor but they  spent all of their money basically on  putting the three of us kids I have two  sisters through private school so any  money that they made basically poured  into our education and as a result we  didn't have you know money for other  things and  um where my friends at these fancy  schools were getting you know BMWs for  their 16th birthday so they can go off  and drive uh you know I didn't get any  of that and it's not what was me but  it's more I just had a scarce mentality  around money in my first business I was  making 300 bucks a month I was eating  the same bean salad lunch every day  because it would fill me up and wasn't  very expensive  when we celebrated a win we'd go to  McDonald's if we got a new client like  hey we sold another piece of our  software we go to McDonald's and Order  large fries and share that between the  three of us because it was cheap and we  wanted just some little way to celebrate  and  I just remember how painful it was to  feel like you have no money and you  can't buy stuff and I couldn't hang out  with my friends and I couldn't do what I  wanted to do and I think that has a  traumatic effect you know I mean maybe  that's you as well you you have a  scarcity mindset around money that you  don't know how to make it and so  anything you've got you got to really  hold on to it and protect it  and again I'm not advocating for being  Reckless or stupid or just throwing  money away be smart about how you're  going to invest and use your money the  more important thing is developing the  mindset that you can  create money that by bringing a lot of  value to people you can make more money  you can turn it into something  so one of the things that I've done  recently that that has helped both  myself and Nina my wife is we create  what we call a care fund  and every month when we're doing our  numbers  Nina will put together how much we've  made this month how much cash flows come  in ETC and then we allocate a certain  percentage for a care fund that we have  to go off and spend  uh either for ourselves or for other  people  and so my default is to invest invest  invest invest invest right like invest  back into the business invest into into  into markets invest in the assets just  invest invest invest invest invest  invest  the that's a good that's a great good  mindset the downside of that is you  don't get to see  the impact that it can create  and so said you know what we need to  dedicate a percentage every month to go  and help somebody else and maybe it's  help ourselves you know  um on the weekend Nina bought a very  expensive purse  we went shopping she had a very  offensive purse we bought a Chanel bag  and  probably more expensive than she's ever  bought a bag and for me it's like oh my  gosh you can't be spending this amount  of money on a bag  but it's worth  celebrating yourself so you know what  like we earned that we did so much work  in our business you can you can go and  afford that  we've also used the money to donate the  Charities we've also used the money to  uh support our family and things that  they needed or wanted in their lives and  it's something that we have to spend  every month  Nina asked hey can we just save it so we  can invest more and then that leads to  more in the future like no we're already  saving other money to do that like that  has to be spent every month and so where  we have to sit this might sound crazy we  have to sit down every month and figure  out how are we going to spend this money  because my default is not to go and  spend the default is to invest or just  to save  and so doing that it doesn't have to be  a big amount of money it could it could  be 100 bucks a month that you force  yourself to spend on making somebody  else's life better or even your own like  that thing that you would never buy for  yourself you know what I've worked hard  like I'm gonna buy it or you're gonna go  buy somebody a meal or you're gonna go  and give a homeless person a hundred  dollars right like you're gonna you're  gonna do something with it  because what it does it starts to change  your mentality around it it starts to  make you feel like  more will come  that I'm creating  and so whether it's 10 bucks 100 bucks a  thousand bucks 10 000 bucks like you  know whatever it is I'm not advocating  you go drain your bank account and just  go crazy and buy a Chanel bag you know  but allocating a certain percentage  every month  so that you can start to rewire your  beliefs around money that it's not just  super scarce so that would be step  number one right allocate some kind of  budget to helping especially others  because when you can when you help  others it just makes you feel so good  and you can help others in a lot of ways  you can help them with your time you can  help them with your expertise y